// endpoint_resolve_peer_delivery.proto — ResolvePeerDelivery: WHICH SESSIONS
// are the two ends of one cross-session message, by the vendor's delivery id
// for it.
//
// WHY THE DAEMON ASKS A SHIM. The daemon draws each end's row of a message
// between two Claude sessions and names the session at the other end. The
// delivery id is the one value both ends' records share
// (conversation.v1.PeerDeliveryId), and both records are in the host's one
// store, which the daemon never reads directly: its read path is this service.
// Any running shim can answer, because the store is shared by every session on
// the host; the shim asks the store and relays.

